---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Cookie Policy - Leaders In Incentives, Rewards & Loyalty Programs | GRG India"
  description="Read GRG India's Cookie Policy to understand how we use cookies and similar tracking technologies on www.grgindia.in."
  canonical="https://www.grgindia.in/cookie-policy/"
>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-navy mb-2">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">GRG India — Tajonline India Private Limited. Last updated: September 3, 2026</p>

      <div class="prose prose-lg text-gray-700 space-y-6">
        <p>
          This Cookie Policy explains how Tajonline India Private Limited, trading as GRG India ("GRG India", "we", "us", "our"), uses cookies and similar tracking technologies on <a href="https://www.grgindia.in" class="text-brand hover:underline">www.grgindia.in</a> (the "Website"). It should be read together with our <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="text-brand hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          By clicking "Accept All" on our cookie banner, you consent to the use of cookies as described below. You may also choose "Necessary Only" to limit cookies to those essential for the Website to function.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mt-10">1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. They allow the website to recognize your device, remember your preferences, and collect information about how the site is used. Similar technologies covered by this policy include web beacons, pixels, and local storage.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mt-10">2. Types of Cookies We Use</h2>
        <p><strong>a) Strictly Necessary Cookies.</strong> These cookies are essential for the Website to function properly — for example, enabling secure areas of the site, load balancing, or remembering your cookie consent choice. These cannot be switched off and do not require consent, as they are necessary to provide the Website.</p>
        <p><strong>b) Performance & Analytics Cookies.</strong> These cookies help us understand how visitors interact with the Website (e.g., pages visited, time spent, error messages) so we can measure and improve site performance. These are only set with your consent ("Accept All").</p>
        <p><strong>c) Functional Cookies.</strong> These cookies remember choices you make (such as language or region) to provide a more personalized experience. Set only with your consent, where used.</p>
        <p><strong>d) Targeting / Advertising Cookies.</strong> These cookies may be used to track visitors across websites to display relevant advertising or measure the effectiveness of marketing campaigns. Set only with your consent, where used.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mt-10">3. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Some cookies on our Website are placed by third-party service providers — specifically Google Analytics (site analytics) and Google Ads (conversion tracking), and by embedded content or demo-booking tools where used. These third parties may collect information about your online activities over time and across different websites. Their use of cookies is governed by their own privacy and cookie policies, which we encourage you to review.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mt-10">4. Cookie List</h2>
        <p>
          The table below reflects the tracking mechanisms configured in the Website's own code as of the date above. Google Analytics and Google Ads set their own cookies directly in your browser once consent is granted; the exact cookie names, values, and durations for those are determined by Google and can change without action on our part, so we've named the category and provider rather than guessing at specifics we can't verify from our side. For the current definitive list of cookies Google sets, see Google's own cookie documentation.
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-300 text-left">
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-navy">Cookie / Storage Item</th>
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-navy">Type</th>
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-navy">Purpose</th>
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-navy">Duration</th>
                <th class="py-2 font-semibold text-navy">Provider</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">cookie-consent</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Strictly Necessary</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Remembers your cookie consent choice (stored via browser local storage, not a traditional cookie)</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Until cleared by you</td>
                <td class="py-2">GRG India (first-party)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Google Analytics (GA4) cookies</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Performance & Analytics</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Distinguishes and tracks visitors for site analytics</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Set by Google — see Google's cookie documentation</td>
                <td class="py-2">Google Analytics</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Google Ads conversion cookies</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Targeting / Advertising</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Measures conversions from Google Ads campaigns</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Set by Google — see Google's cookie documentation</td>
                <td class="py-2">Google Ads</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
          This list reflects the tracking tools wired into the Website's code. It is not the output of a browser-level cookie audit, and we'll update it if that scope changes.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mt-10">5. How to Manage Your Cookie Preferences</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>5.1 On our Website:</strong> You can accept or limit non-essential cookies using the cookie consent banner shown when you first visit the Website. At present, the Website does not have a persistent "Cookie Preferences" control to reopen the banner after your initial choice. To change a previous choice, you can clear your browser's local storage and cookies for grgindia.in, which will cause the banner to appear again on your next visit.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>5.2 Through your browser:</strong> Most browsers allow you to control cookies through their settings, including blocking or deleting cookies. Please note that disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of the Website. Guidance is generally available in your browser's help section (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge, etc.).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>5.3 Opting out of analytics:</strong> Where Google Analytics or similar tools are used, you may opt out using the provider's dedicated opt-out tools (e.g., the Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on).
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mt-10">6. Legal Basis & Consent</h2>
        <p>
          Where required under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and other applicable law, we rely on your consent to set non-essential cookies, obtained via the consent banner on the Website. You may withdraw consent at any time by adjusting your cookie preferences or browser settings, without affecting the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy mt-10">7. Changes to This Cookie Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the cookies we use or for operational, legal, or regulatory reasons. Material changes will be notified via a prominent notice on the Website.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
